{"content":[{"c":["HARAR, HARARITE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Terms applied to several names that appear in the accounts of King David’s “mighty men.” Shammah, one of David’s mightiest men, and Jonathan’s father (a different Jonathan than Saul’s son and David’s friend) is called a Hararite (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.11,33","r":"2Sam.23.11,33","rawR":"2Sam.23.11,33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.11,33","value":"2Sam.23.11,33"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:11, 33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.34","r":"1Chr.11.34","rawR":"1Chr.11.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.34","value":"1Chr.11.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:34"}," has “Shagee”), as is Agee, Shammah’s father (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.11","r":"2Sam.23.11","rawR":"2Sam.23.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.11","value":"2Sam.23.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:11"},"). Sharar, Ahiam’s father, is also so named (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.33","r":"2Sam.23.33","rawR":"2Sam.23.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.33","value":"2Sam.23.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.35","r":"1Chr.11.35","rawR":"1Chr.11.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.35","value":"1Chr.11.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:35"}," has “Sachar”). The meaning of the terms are uncertain; possibly “mountain” from the location of a village (Harar) or “mountaineer.”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HararHararite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:11, 33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.11,33","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.11,33","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.11,33"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.34","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.34","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.34"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.11","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.11","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.11"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.33","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.33","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.33"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.35","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.35","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.35"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ac63d87b44acf952beb5030f25070734fcce106f0e80bf993f6ad17973c6c2be","sourceItemName":"HararHararite","sourceItemOrder":107,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HararHararite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Harar, Hararite*","title":"Harar, Hararite*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}